 or enforcement linkage under D03. Retain that linkage uncertainty rather than treating every audit or proposed adjustment as an investigation or excluding it conclusively."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Marriott: consumer litigation concerning the same Starwood Data Security Incident","event_dates":["2025-06-03"],"reported_context_times":["loss accrual as of: 2025-12-31"],"status":"PRIVATE_LITIGATION_AND_MEDIATION","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:99502d9018e934545c8936a7b69c62e3bea7a4d8112359818b309b54b95fcd58","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":1313},{"unit_id":"sha256:99502d9018e934545c8936a7b69c62e3bea7a4d8112359818b309b54b95fcd58","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":1316}],"description":"Approximately 100 consumer and other lawsuits followed the incident in U.S. and Canadian courts. The Fourth Circuit reversed class certification on June 3, 2025; some plaintiffs then sued individually in New York. Marriott has engaged in MDL mediation and is defending the claims; a loss accrual is reported at December 31, 2025. Courts and private plaintiffs do not establish a governmental investigation."},{"kind":"PRIVATE_OR_INTERNAL_ACTION","subject":"Marriott: third-party intellectual-property claims","event_dates":[],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"CURRENT_PRIVATE_LEGAL_PROCEEDINGS","evidence":[{"unit_id":"sha256:c602ecc69500ffb50c421970157577cb6e31c757c5bbb45f15ae8dc5e7fc7fc1","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":376},{"unit_id":"sha256:99502d9018e934545c8936a7b69c62e3bea7a4d8112359818b309b54b95fcd58","kind":"VISIBLE_BLOCK","source_index":1322}],"description":"Marriott expressly is currently party to infringement claims brought by others. No governmental investigative actor or enforcement relation is established; current private litigation does not become a current D03 action."},{"kind":"OTHER_MEANING","subject":"Marriott: internal information-security incident investigation","event_dates":[],"reported_context_times":[],"status":"INTERNAL_INCID